---
import AppShell from "@/components/AppShell.astro";
import PencilSkyline from "@/components/PencilSkyline.astro";

// The start page names the product and says what it is for (`S-08`). It still says nothing
// else: no feature cards, no second sign-in button — the topbar already carries that, so the
// page describes and admits in the same breath.
//
// What changed here on 2026-08-05 is only the paint. `S-08` recorded "the cosmic styling
// stays" as an explicit decision; the product owner reversed it, and the orbs, the star field
// and the gradient-clipped wordmark went with the rest of the starter's vocabulary. The pencil
// drawing below arrived the same day and is the one picture in the product — the component
// carries the argument for why it is a drawing rather than a photograph.
//
// `nav={false}` keeps the module rail off this page even for a signed-in reader: this is the
// public face of the product, and the drawing is the only thing here that should be competing
// for attention.
---

<AppShell title="EstateManager" nav={false}>
  <div class="flex flex-col items-center py-16 text-center sm:py-20">
    <h1 class="text-foreground text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">EstateManager</h1>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-4 max-w-xl text-lg">Twój portal do zarządzania nieruchomościami</p>

    <div class="mt-12 w-full max-w-2xl">
      <PencilSkyline />
    </div>
  </div>
</AppShell>
